Verified against the exact installed version, not upstream HEAD. `dpkg -l` shows `ros-jazzy-spatio-temporal-voxel-layer 2.5.5-1noble.20260615.174701`; rosdistro `jazzy/distribution.yaml` pins `spatio_temporal_voxel_layer` at `2.5.5-1` from `SteveMacenski/spatio_temporal_voxel_layer`. I cloned the `jazzy` branch (package.xml `<version>2.5.5</version>`) to /tmp/claude-1000/-home-myhome-YBNML/691d883b-bd7f-499c-9b36-a59b0bd14a8a/scratchpad/stvl_jazzy. Binary fingerprint confirms source==binary: `strings /opt/ros/jazzy/lib/libspatio_temporal_voxel_layer_core.so` contains the upstream typo `"Passthough filter activated."` plus `min_obstacle_height`/`max_obstacle_height`. I also diffed against ros2/HEAD (2.6.0) — this logic is byte-identical, so the claim is not version-sensitive.

PRIMARY SOURCE 1 — spatio_temporal_voxel_layer/src/measurement_buffer.cpp (2.5.5), `BufferROSCloud()`. Transform first, filter second:
    // transform the cloud in the global frame
    tf2::doTransform(cloud, *cld_global, tf_stamped);
    ...
    } else if (_filter == Filters::PASSTHROUGH) {
      pass_through_filter.setFilterFieldName("z");
      pass_through_filter.setFilterLimits(_min_obstacle_height, _max_obstacle_height);
The VOXEL branch does the same via `sor.setFilterFieldName("z"); sor.setFilterLimits(_min_obstacle_height, _max_obstacle_height);`. `_min_obstacle_height`/`_max_obstacle_height` are plain `double` members (measurement_buffer.hpp:161).

PRIMARY SOURCE 2 — spatio_temporal_voxel_layer/src/spatio_temporal_voxel_layer.cpp:77:
    _global_frame = std::string(layered_costmap_->getGlobalFrameID());
passed to the MeasurementBuffer ctor as the target frame. Defaults declared at the same file: `min_obstacle_height` 0.0, `max_obstacle_height` 3.0, `filter` "passthrough". Dynamic reconfigure handled at the `name_ + "." + source + "." + "min_obstacle_height"` / `max_obstacle_height` branches near line 848/859.

PRIMARY SOURCE 3 — same file, `UpdateROSCostmap()`: marks come from `_voxel_grid->GetFlattenedCostmap()`, iterating `occupany_cell{x, y}` and writing `costmap_[getIndex(map_x, map_y)] = nav2_costmap_2d::LETHAL_OBSTACLE` when the column count passes `_mark_threshold`. The 3D grid is flattened by (x,y) with z discarded — so the global-frame z passthrough is the ONLY height discrimination anywhere in the plugin. A grep for `min_obstacle_height|max_obstacle_height` across the whole package returns only the buffer ctor, the two PCL filter calls, the two setters, and the param declarations — no ground-plane or terrain-relative code path exists.

PRIMARY SOURCE 4 — project ground truth, /home/myhome/YBNML/sim/models/orchard_terrain/heightmap_meta.json: `"terrace_steps": [0.3798, 0.3316, 0.375, 0.2734, 0.4762, 0.4974, 0.2647, 0.3396, 0.4325]`, `"profile": "terraced_random"`, `"rows": 10`, `"face_width": 1.2`, `"ramp_len": 4.5`, `"noise_amp": 0.025`. /home/myhome/YBNML/scripts/gen_heightmap.py `build_terrace_levels()` makes them monotonic: `levels = np.concatenate([[0.0], np.cumsum(steps)])`. Sum = 3.3702 m. The 0.80 m draft window appears in /home/myhome/YBNML/docs/research/02-nav2-apple-disease.md as `min_obstacle_height: 0.20, max_obstacle_height: 1.00`.

PRIMARY SOURCE 5 (for the escape-hatch caveat) — gz-math `include/gz/math/DiffDriveOdometry.hh` exposes only `X()`, `Y()`, `Heading()`, `LinearVelocity()`, `AngularVelocity()`; no z, roll or pitch state. /home/myhome/YBNML/ros2_ws/src/orchard_sim/orchard_sim/gt_localizer.py composes `T_map_odom = T_map_base @ invert(T_odom_base)` from that planar wheel odometry, so the z offset is absorbed into map→odom and `odom` is not z-fixed in the current sim rig.
